{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_research_rotation_endpoint_and_port_model_is_broken_bug4_base_port_endpoint", "label": "Bug 4 \u2014 after a Role-A cutover nothing durable can address the active tun", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/rotation-endpoint-and-port-model-is-broken.md", "source_location": "reconcile.rs:116-147, state.rs:80-82, db.rs:2932-2962", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "device_config_pinned can only select live_endpoints or primary_endpoint(), and neither can ever carry an offset port; the only offset-port producers are two transient writers that guess, on mutually incompatible models, both made unfounded by T3's free-list plan_port. The one-sided path survives only by accident of the change-guard rendering identically and never rewriting the device."}, {"id": "docs_research_rotation_endpoint_and_port_model_is_broken_bug5_second_rotation_cannot_complete", "label": "Bug 5 \u2014 the SECOND rotation cannot complete", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/rotation-endpoint-and-port-model-is-broken.md", "source_location": "crates/wiremesh-gateway/tests/key_rotation.rs", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "No test has ever rotated twice \u2014 every case goes 0\u21921 once from a clean tree. A gateway never returns to the base port after a cutover, so on 1\u21922 our tun dials peer:51822 while the peer's overlap dials our retiring 51821; unlike 0\u21921 there is no correctly-dialing side to roam from. A fabric-wide outage on the SECOND timer fire, hidden behind any fix for the first."}, {"id": "docs_research_rotation_endpoint_and_port_model_is_broken_role_b_collapse_never_completes", "label": "The Role-B collapse can never complete after any Role-A cutover", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/rotation-endpoint-and-port-model-is-broken.md", "source_location": "main.rs:4784-4788", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The collapse waits for an rx-corroborated session on the active tun toward the peer's new key, but that tun's peer entry points at the peer's base port, which after retire is nothing \u2014 the F9 leak shape, reachable on the currently-green one-sided path and visible only because the in-step done-bar added the settle-to-1 gauge assertion."}, {"id": "docs_research_rotation_endpoint_and_port_model_is_broken_rotation_interval_off_mitigation", "label": "WIREMESH_ROTATION_INTERVAL=off \u2014 automatic rotation disabled fabric-wide", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/research/rotation-endpoint-and-port-model-is-broken.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Landed in v0.7.0 (PR #47) and set on the live px controller 2026-08-05, defusing the scheduled 2026-08-31 outage. Do not re-enable until the single port authority exists and a rotate-twice test is green."}, {"id": "docs_research_rotation_endpoint_and_port_model_is_broken_single_port_authority", "label": "Fix shape \u2014 one port authority (per-peer endpoint-override pin)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/research/rotation-endpoint-and-port-model-is-broken.md", "source_location": "reconcile.rs:112-115", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Remove the divergence rather than repair the guess: one renderer for the device so no apply can drift, reconciling device_config_at_port and pending_peer_configs against it. Advertising the active port in local_endpoints was rejected (observed candidate always sorts first, the observe socket is pinned for process life, set_local_candidates is a destructive REPLACE, and under NAT the new socket has no punched mapping); teaching device_config_pinned the offset was rejected (no source of truth exists at the moment it is needed)."}, {"id": "docs_research_rotation_endpoint_and_port_model_is_broken_ground_truth_endpoint_feedback", "label": "Fix shape \u2014 ground-truth endpoint feedback from boringtun's get=1", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/research/rotation-endpoint-and-port-model-is-broken.md", "source_location": "uapi.rs:344-372", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "parse_get_response currently drops the per-peer endpoint= line that reflects the roamed value; seeding live_endpoints from it at cutover makes every later recompute reproduce reality so the guard stops lying. Smaller and self-correcting; composes with the single port authority."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_research_rotation_endpoint_and_port_model_is_broken_bug4_base_port_endpoint", "target": "docs_research_rotation_endpoint_and_port_model_is_broken_bug5_second_rotation_cannot_complete", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/research/rotation-endpoint-and-port-model-is-broken.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_research_rotation_endpoint_and_port_model_is_broken_bug4_base_port_endpoint", "target": "docs_research_key_rotation_teardown_notes_finding_a_base_port_endpoint_churn", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/research/rotation-endpoint-and-port-model-is-broken.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_research_rotation_endpoint_and_port_model_is_broken_bug5_second_rotation_cannot_complete", "target": "docs_research_rotation_fixes_review_findings_tunnel_id_namespace_split", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/research/rotation-endpoint-and-port-model-is-broken.md", "source_location": "plan_port free-list", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_research_rotation_endpoint_and_port_model_is_broken_role_b_collapse_never_compl